	As requested, and with the author's permission, I am posting a
	uuencoded copy (in 2 parts) of ARC5.LBR.  It will be posted to
	net.micro.pc.  This MS-DOS library contains the following:

		ARC.EQE		SQueezed executable
		ARC.DQC		SQueezed documentation

	You will need a copy of a MS-DOS LU (library utility) to
	extract the squeezed files, and a copy of an MS-DOS file
	UNSQueezer to decompress them.  These can be found on 
	numerous BBS.

	To use what follows:
		1 - Remove the header and any trailing space that
		    are a artifact of the USENET/UUCP mail process.
		2 - Cat the 2 parts together.
		3 - Run uudecode against the concatenated file to
		    generate ARC5.LBR
		4 - Use your favorite comm program to move ARC5.LBR
		    to your personal computer.
		5 - Then use the appropriate MS-DOS (or PC-DOS)
		    utilities to extract the library and unsqueeze
		    the files.  Look over the documentation.  Looks
		    like some time and effort went into them.


